/*
  core/masks/busy_share.spthy -- f_H for the Busy mask, SHARE_PW action.

  The SLIP failure for password sharing (distinct from Careless's in-band leak): a rushed Busy
  user fat-fingers the side-channel address and sends the passphrase to the WRONG recipient. The
  guide notes envelope/recipient metadata is unprotected -- a misdirected secret. We model the
  wrong address as adversary-reachable (Out), and crucially NO Oob reaches the intended recipient,
  so the outcome is doubly bad: the secret leaks AND the legitimate recipient is locked out
  (no silent success -- a visible delivery failure). MisdeliveredPw(P) marks it. RespMask(P,'Busy')
  is gated by mask_state.spthy: Busy must be the current mask (set by sigma3 TimePressure on share).
*/

rule Share_Busy_slip:
    [ !Req(P, rid, 'SHARE_PW', <recip, pw>, c) ]
  --[ Share(P,'Busy'), RespMask(P,'Busy'), Answered(rid),
      MisdeliveredPw(P), Mask(P,'Attentive','Busy') ]->
    [ Out(pw) ]
